# Auto commit & push

Whenever you make changes in this application (code, styles, assets, config, or project rules):

1. **Commit** those changes yourself when the work for that request is done — do not wait for the user to ask.
2. **Push** the commit to the GitHub remote (`origin`) yourself after a successful commit.
3. Follow the normal commit safety protocol (status/diff/log, HEREDOC message, no force-push to main/master, no secrets, no `--no-verify` unless asked).
4. Skip empty commits. Include relevant untracked project files; ignore noise like `.DS_Store` unless the user wants it.
5. After pushing, briefly confirm the commit message and that the push succeeded (include the remote branch if useful).

This project rule **overrides** the default “only commit when asked” user preference **for this repository only**.
